80 million years ago dinosaurs ruled the  surface of planet Earth yet in the blink  of a cosmic eye this Kingdom would fall  to a mass extinction and an entirely  unexpected order of animals would take  their place if a similar Calamity were  to upend Nature's order once again what  kinds of incredible life forms might  emerge set 80 million years from now the  soul cash bestieri is a speculative  biology project by the brilliant artist  and World Builder Terry Miranda  through naturalist style illustrations  it explores a world where Humanity has  long disappeared and evolution has  drastically transformed the animals we  know today  so for this entry into the archive we'll  explore this reborn Earth and as always  you can support the artist on patreon to  see more of the project using the links  in the description now let's travel to  the distant future and discover the  creatures of the soulcash bestiary  80 million years from now the island of  solkesh is a land mass where the  extremes of the environment meet the  extremes of evolution today some of the  most extreme ecosystems are coral reefs  in the era of soulcash coral has adapted  to thrive in the intertidal zone  allowing familiar Reef life to take to  the land  one of the first pioneers of these  semi-terrestrial reefs is the tentacled  seraphal this semi-aquatic cephalopod  creeps from the ocean as the Tide Falls  feeding on mollusks and Crustaceans left  exposed to the sun incredible as this  might sound we already have some  documentation of cephalopods moving upon  the land in a limited capacity and while  the seraphole is technically more  closely related to Modern squids than  octopus 80 million years is plenty of  time for such a creature to emerge given  the right conditions seraphal tentacles  have hardened into claw-like tips for  dragging their body across the land and  for cracking open the shells of urchins  and crabs so they can Feast for like  their squid ancestors seropholes or  carnivores  but there are larger carnivores in these  reborn reefs the lancelet is a  slithering Terror that searches for The  Telltale rhythm of prey with their  sensitive antennae perhaps unexpectedly  these Ambush Predators or the  descendants of the lethargic sea slug  yet in the era of soulcash the lancelots  can move with whip-like speed able to  launch themselves at prey with deadly  accuracy and spear them with their  forward-facing prongs in the arms race  of evolution these reefs are a war zone  surveying the battlefield with their  solitary orange eye the gorill is one  particularly alien creature with four  loping limbs they stride across the sand  feeding on anything the tide dredges up  remarkably these slimy carnivores are  the descendants of mollusks although  they've evolved fleshy limbs convergent  with other land animals their unique  method of digestion produces a pearl of  sorts in their gullet made from  compressed bone when threatened by a  fearsome Predator they can expel this  Cannonball like Pearl with devastating  Force  and few predators are as fearsome as the  day lash these Serpentine Hunters live  together upon hatching and when emerging  from their Burrows resemble multi-headed  hydras an offshoot of today's Garden  eels they've retained their ancestors  habit of peeking out of the sand in  unison with exceptionally large eyes the  day lash can track and snatch up most  any stray fish that tumbles through the  current with their trap-like jaws yet  these dalash are only juveniles  Adult Day lash are large enough to hunt  alone these full-grown Terrors are  expert Hunters able to Brave a wide  variety of environments like modern  moray eels they are experts at  navigating tight corners and lashing out  from hidden Caverns to ensnare prey the  dalash or further proof that this new  reef environment is a realm of fearsome  competition  moving Inland the shore gives way to a  mosaic of swampland in our era swamps  and other Wetlands only cover around  seven percent of Earth's surface yet are  home to numerous unique life forms that  have adapted to both land and water and  80 million years in the future many of  these animals look quite different  rising to the height of a large dog the  soul Mundus slinks through the wetlands  hunting for prey while this amphibian  has become a feared Ambush predator in  the shallow ponds of these swamps their  ancestor is none other than the humble  lungless salamander the Sol mundus's  tongue is tipped with a deadly bone spur  that sits beneath their skull while at  rest to hunt the soul Mundus lashes out  with this spear-like tongue to impale  and quickly retract their prey into a  gluttonous needle-toothed Maw  in the impenetrable murk of the waters  that flood The Woodlands the murrows  sensed their surroundings clearly though  blind these gargantuan fish use their  many sensitive whiskers in combination  with low voltage electrical pulses to  detect the movement of prey much like  how their ancestors the catfish do today  creatures outside the water are equally  unsafe as this Predator can quickly  breach the opaque surface with a  vacuum-like gulp with prey instantly  disappearing into the murrow's gullet as  they sink back contently into the thick  silt  roaming in small herds across the tidal  Flats the pebbleback awk show that some  mammals still persist in this strange  future while these sheep-like creatures  might seem out of place in a swampy  environment they are well adapted for a  lifestyle that's a bit soggier than what  most mammals would put up with despite  their appearance the awk are actually a  highly derived offshoots of the  hippopotamus which are already  semi-aquatic to stay safe while wading  into Dangerous Waters the orc possess a  wide crest of horns and rows of hardened  osteoderms to deter Predators for  nightmarish creatures lurk in the depths  of the swamp  in the Sullen green light of the kelp  forest the larkira slides through the  tall 