kness these eel-like  creatures can search for the faintest  pulse of heat from prey using highly  sensitive heat pits along the sides of  their head having evolved from snakes  that became accustomed to life in the  dark pits over Millennia the cranas  haven't lost the Venom of their  predecessors to administer their  venomous strike the cranus possesses  forward-facing fangs they use to spear  their prey in the narrow tunnels of the  Underground  in the deepest Limestone caves the  enormous tarakni reign supreme a mighty  arachnid the tarachni uses its powerful  front limbs to break through the tough  shells of its preferred prey while today  the size of spiders is limited by the  level of oxygen in Earth's atmosphere  arthropods in the soulcash timeline have  evolved a more efficient means of  respiration allowing them to grow to  sizes not seen since the Carboniferous  period  extensive channels of spherical openings  provide the turokni with extra oxygen  giving it the fuel needed to support its  thick exoskeleton in armored limbs  back on the surface a mighty  uninterrupted grassland stretches across  much of soulcash in our era grasslands  are home to some of the largest land  animals on our planet 80 million years  into the future a new kingdom of giants  might emerge  slowly plotting across the flower fields  of Western soulcash the mighty Rue  towards churn up the Earth in search of  deep soil tubers protected from  predators by a thick external shell  these herbivores are unlike any of the  megafauna seen on The Plains today for  root warts or another distant relative  of arthropods able to grow far larger  than their ancestors due to their highly  efficient oxygen intake in a more  complex internal support structure and  thanks to their docile temperament  certain birds have learned to nest on  the backs of these mild mannered Giants  amid the footsteps of the behemoths the  quick pitter-patter of Talon feet  resonates over the dry plains as the  axolot 